ecialty industrial applications in the United States, China, South Korea, Japan, Taiwan, Singapore, and internationally. The company operates through Vacuum Solutions Division (VSD), Photonics Solutions Division (PSD), and Material Solutions Division (MSD) segments. Its VSD segment provides foundational technology solutions, including pressure measurement and control, flow measurement and control, gas and vapor delivery, gas composition analysis, electronic control technology, reactive gas generation and delivery, power generation and delivery, and fiber optic temperature and position sensing. The PSD segment offers range of solutions, which include lasers, photonics, optics, precision motion control, and vibration control. Its MSD segment develops, process, and manufactures technologies comprising advanced surface modification, electroless and electrolytic plating, and surface finishing for chemistry, equipment, and services markets, as well as high-technology applications. In addition, the company sells its products and services through direct sales, network of independent distributors, and sales representatives, as well as websites, including product catalogs. MKS Inc. was formerly known as MKS Instruments, Inc. and changed its name to MKS Inc. in May 2025. The company was incorporated in 1961 and is based in Andover, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. John T. C. Lee Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 62 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $385K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 11%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $49K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["MKS Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $14.6B market cap on $3.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +17% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 45%.","The business throws off $497M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 13 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.19\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $21.6M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-21551886.88},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"MKS (MKSI) Reliance on International Sales: What Investors Need to Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3029384/mks-mksi-reliance-on-international-sales-what-investors-need-to-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_international_revenues-3029384","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575711.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MKS (MKSI) Stock Looks In Line With Fair Value On Record AI Demand","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-mksi/mks/news/mks-mksi-stock-looks-in-line-with-fair-value-on-record-ai-de","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794569337.065,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.9,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Comparing ASML (NASDAQ:ASML) and MKS (NASDAQ:MKSI)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/comparing-asml-nasdaqasml-and-mks-nasdaqmksi.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794479364.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MKS Inc. $MKSI Stake Lessened by Retirement Systems of Alabama","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/mks-inc-mksi-stake-lessened-by-retirement-systems-of-alabama.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794395165.0,"o